|passage=sentences not of '''ephemeral''', but of eternal, efficacy}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1818|author=Mary Shelley|title=Frankenstein|chapter=9|url=http://ebooks.adelaide.edu.au/s/shelley/mary/s53f/chapter9.html|passage=It was during an access of this kind that I suddenly left my home, and bending my steps towards the near Alpine valleys, sought in the magnificence, the eternity of such scenes, to forget myself and my '''ephemeral''', because human, sorrows.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120403120050/http://ebooks.adelaide.edu.au/s/shelley/mary/s53f/chapter9.html|archivedate=3 April 2012}}
