==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂yew-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|justice}}, from {{der|en|fro|justise}}, {{m|fro|justice}} (Modern {{cog|fr|justice}}), from {{der|en|la|iūstitia|t=righteousness, equity}}, from {{m|la|iūstus|t=just}}, from {{m|la|iūs|t=right}}, from {{der|en|itc-pro|*jowos}}, perhaps literally "sacred formula", a word peculiar to Latin (not general Italic) that originated in the religious cults, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂yew-}}. {{doublet|en|Justitia}}.

Partly displaced native {{ncog|ang|rihtwīsnes}} ({{w|Modern English}} {{m|en|righteousness}} < {{m|en|rightwiseness}}).

